After my wizard ascension, I decided try a rogue next (as per Jove's
recommendation). I found it easy, almost too easy. It took me six
tries, which is a lot less than the 70+ tries it took me to ascend a
wizard.

However, I had a moment where I almost ruined this game. Juiblex
engulfed me, I got out and killed it without breaking a sweat. However,
it was late, I was tired and so I failed to notice I was  deathly
sick... Next thing I notice is that my "oLS glows and grumbles to dust.
Luckily I had couple of those already at that point.

And soon after I removed my ring of levitation in order to dilute some
potions in a fountain at Juiblex's swamp. Didn't remember to put the
ring back on, so I stepped straight into water and sunk,
unintentionally creating lots of diluted potions and empty scrolls...
So I had to climb back up to my stash to get potion of oil (had 15
rusty +7 daggers), use a wish for another magic marker and rewrite the
scrolls I felt I needed (charging for /oD's, gold detection and
genocide).

Another minor setback was, that Baalzebub escaped me reading a C?oT. I
didn't bother to look for it, so I had to kill it on my ascension run.
Partly because of that, the run was slow. I also had to kill Rodney 8
times, twice it was "Double Trouble" time.

I had to read the spoilers in order to finish the quest. The rogue
quest is ridiculous IMO.

I found my first filthy nest, no eggs however.

Previously I've had most difficulties with plane of air. Now I had a
tooled horn with me, so I had no problems whatsoever with air
elementals.

Found the right altar at first try. Yay!

Daggers and expert skill make the game almost too easy, so I'm going to
try something else next. But what? Maybe a monk or a healer, or a
knight with wishless/genoless conduct.

